    Bug 2059370 - Test the conflict prompt the offline synchronization raises. r=mkmelin

    `calCachedCalendar._doSynchronize` asks through `cal.provider.promptOverwrite()`
    when the server copy has moved on since an offline change. That was untested:
    the prompt is modal, so a test reaching it hangs xpcshell.

    Stub the dialog the way `test_caldav_requests.js` does and cover the three
    branches around it - an offline modification and an offline deletion that lose
    the race against the server, and an offline modification of an event the server
    has deleted. Each checks the mode, the copy handed over, and what either answer
    leaves behind on both sides. The stub is registered for the whole file, so the
    existing tasks now assert that a sync without a competing server change asks
    nothing at all.

    The server copy needs a stamp in the future to win, because storing an offline
    edit restamps the item. An offline deletion does not restamp it.

    The dialog itself stays out of reach here and was checked by hand instead. It
    appears when it should and both answers do what they say; its wording is not
    always right. That run is written up in this bug, follow-ups are filed.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317045

